  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>}</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>}</mo></math></p><p>Now, Graph of min&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>}</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/097a4854-839b-4efd-bb7a-a0bcbb3b4455-image.png\" style=\"width: 326px; height: 250px;\" /></p><p>Clearly graph is continuous in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>]</mo></math> but non differentiable at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math> points (i.e. greater than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>) in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p>",
